  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1222 PM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nSimilar to the short term, the extended portion continues to \nfeature plenty of sun, above normal high temperatures and \nrelatively comfortable mornings. This changes by Sunday as a\ndry trough moves over our area. As this happens, we then begin to\nlose the influence of the high pressure over us with a return to \nonshore flow. This likely means the return of humid days along \nwith warmer high temperatures. While onshore flow returns by \nSunday many across the area likely won't feel the true effects of \nthis flow until Monday. By that point we could be looking at highs\nin the low to perhaps mid 90s. Add in the increasing moisture and\nwe could see heat indices close to 100 degrees and even \napproaching 105 degrees by middle of next week. Enjoy the upcoming\npleasant days through the first half of this weekend as warm and \nhumid days look to once again make a return across the area.",
